 "result_text": "Equation fields now use Knack's own formatted value for `.formatted`, so the days figure (4 and 5 in your examples) is kept instead of the raw seconds. I haven't run the tests or tried it against real data.\n\nThe fix is one line in `knackpy/models.py`: I added `\"equation\": {\"use_knack_format\": True}` to `FIELD_SETTINGS`. `Record._handle_fields` then passes Knack's formatted value through to `Field`. The default formatter returns it as-is. `.raw` is unchanged and still holds the seconds value (e.g. `372171.318\u2026`).\n\nA formatted value of exactly `0` still falls back to the raw value, because `Field._format` treats it as empty. I left that alone since the fallback is existing behaviour for timer fields too.",
